addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SENNA MAMORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA HISAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRATA, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HISAZUMI, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISOBE, TETSUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOGUCHI, HIROJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OHASHI, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENNA, MAMORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, HISAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic acid salt is deposited on the surface of a solder powder containing Sn and Zn. Alternatively, 0.5 to 10 wt.% of a nonionic surfactant is added to a flux. By a method comprising such a procedure, provided are a lead-free solder powder and solder paste having good soldering characteristics wherein the reaction of an activating component with an alloy component in a flux is suppressed.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Selon cette invention, un sel d'acide organique est déposé à la surface d'une poudre de soudage contenant Sn et Zn. En variante, on ajoute à un flux entre 0,5 et 10 % en poids d'un surfactant non ionique. Le procédé qui comprend cette procédure permet d'obtenir une pâte et une poudre de soudage exemptes de plomb qui possèdent de bonnes caractéristiques de soudage tandis qu'on élimine la réaction d'un composant activant avec un composant d'alliage dans un flux.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>